{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"dbde3b22aa7e9bf250f0b336","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260812-ts-x470d4u-v3-0-c8e266f1663b%40siewert.io/","channels":["linux-arm-kernel","linux-devicetree"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260812-ts-x470d4u-v3-0-c8e266f1663b@siewert.io","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260812-ts-x470d4u-v3-0-c8e266f1663b%40siewert.io/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260812-ts-x470d4u-v3-0-c8e266f1663b@siewert.io"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v3 2/2] ARM: dts: aspeed: add asrock x470d4u bmc","messages":{"8b7dcb07-2dfd-425f-8ff3-06114e45c676@hatter.bewilderbeest.net":{"id":"8b7dcb07-2dfd-425f-8ff3-06114e45c676@hatter.bewilderbeest.net","messageId":"8b7dcb07-2dfd-425f-8ff3-06114e45c676@hatter.bewilderbeest.net","references":["20260812-ts-x470d4u-v3-0-c8e266f1663b@siewert.io","20260812-ts-x470d4u-v3-2-c8e266f1663b@siewert.io"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260812-ts-x470d4u-v3-2-c8e266f1663b@siewert.io","20260812-ts-x470d4u-v3-0-c8e266f1663b@siewert.io"],"author":{"name":"Zev Weiss","address":"zev@bewilderbeest.net"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Tan Siewert","address":"tan@siewert.io"}],"cc":[{"name":"Rob Herring","address":"robh@kernel.org"},{"name":"Krzysztof Kozlowski","address":"krzk+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"Conor Dooley","address":"conor+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"Joel Stanley","address":"joel@jms.id.au"},{"name":"Andrew Jeffery","address":"andrew@codeconstruct.com.au"},{"name":"","address":"devicetree@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-aspeed@lists.ozlabs.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T04:49:16.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T04:49:16.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v3 2/2] ARM: dts: aspeed: add asrock x470d4u bmc","mailingLists":[{"id":"devicetree.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"devicetree.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hi Tan,"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Looks good overall to me, just a couple small notes below..."},{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Wed, Aug 12, 2026 at 01:28:27PM PDT, Tan Siewert wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"The ASRock Rack X470D4U X470D4U is a single-socket X470-based microATX"},{"depth":1,"text":"motherboard for Ryzen processors with an AST2500 BMC and either 32MB or"},{"depth":1,"text":"64MB SPI flash."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"This mainboard exists in three known \"flavors\" which only differ in the"},{"depth":1,"text":"used host NIC, the BMC SPI size and some parts that may be un-populated."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"To allow the use of the full SPI flash, add two trees, one of which has"},{"depth":1,"text":"the 32M layout with the base config, and a 64M tree that includes the"},{"depth":1,"text":"base tree."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Tan Siewert <tan@siewert.io>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":"arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/Makefile                  |   2 +"},{"depth":1,"text":".../aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u-data64.dts    |  15 +"},{"depth":1,"text":".../boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u.dts  | 381 +++++++++++++++++++++"},{"depth":1,"text":"3 files changed, 398 insertions(+)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/Makefile b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/Makefile"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 6b68671f9379..e27d33e85fb2 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/Makefile"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/Makefile"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -15,6 +15,8 @@ dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ASPEED) += \\"},{"depth":1,"text":"\taspeed-bmc-asrock-paul-ipmi-card.dtb \\"},{"depth":1,"text":"\taspeed-bmc-asrock-romed8hm3.dtb \\"},{"depth":1,"text":"\taspeed-bmc-asrock-spc621d8hm3.dtb \\"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\taspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u.dtb \\"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\taspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u-data64.dtb \\"},{"depth":1,"text":"\taspeed-bmc-asrock-x570d4u.dtb \\"},{"depth":1,"text":"\taspeed-bmc-asus-kommando-ipmi-card.dtb \\"},{"depth":1,"text":"\taspeed-bmc-asus-x4tf.dtb \\"},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u-data64.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u-data64.dts"},{"depth":1,"text":"new file mode 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 000000000000..6f11aeab087c"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- /dev/null"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u-data64.dts"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@"},{"depth":1,"text":"+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+#include \"aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u.dts\""},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+/ {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tcompatible = \"asrock,x470d4u-data64-bmc\", \"aspeed,ast2500\";"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tmodel = \"Asrock Rack X470D4U-series BMC (64MB store)\";"}],"lineCount":44,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"code","text":"Nit: for consistency with how they spell it, and (at least *most* of) the other aspeed-bmc-asrock-*.dts files, I'd suggest \"ASRock\" instead of \"Asrock\".  (And IMO s/store/flash/ would be a touch clearer.)"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Also, looks like the other nearby DTS files pretty consistently have compatible & model in the opposite order, so matching that might be nice too."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"+};"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+&fmc {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tflash@0 {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t/delete-node/partitions;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+#include \"openbmc-flash-layout-64.dtsi\""},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t};"},{"depth":1,"text":"+};"},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u.dts"},{"depth":1,"text":"new file mode 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 000000000000..80fb2b7c1e0c"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- /dev/null"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u.dts"}],"lineCount":13,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"<snip>"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tfan@3 {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t/* FAN4 (6-pin) */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\treg = <0x03>;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\taspeed,fan-tach-ch = /bits/ 8 <0x03 0x0b>;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t};"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tfan@4 {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t/* FAN5 (6-pin) */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\treg = <0x04>;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\taspeed,fan-tach-ch = /bits/ 8 <0x04 0x0d>;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t};"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tfan@5 {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t/* FAN6 (6-pin) */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\treg = <0x05>;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\taspeed,fan-tach-ch = /bits/ 8 <0x05 0x0e>;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t};"},{"depth":1,"text":"+};"}],"lineCount":19,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Just to confirm, skipping channel 0xc here is intentional I assume?  (Most other related platforms have them contiguously numbered, but not all, so another slight oddity wouldn't be too shocking.)"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thanks,\nZev"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260812-ts-x470d4u-v3-2-c8e266f1663b@siewert.io"},"4e653068-5ef1-47db-8e4e-3b535751e47f@siewert.io":{"id":"4e653068-5ef1-47db-8e4e-3b535751e47f@siewert.io","messageId":"4e653068-5ef1-47db-8e4e-3b535751e47f@siewert.io","references":["20260812-ts-x470d4u-v3-0-c8e266f1663b@siewert.io","20260812-ts-x470d4u-v3-2-c8e266f1663b@siewert.io","8b7dcb07-2dfd-425f-8ff3-06114e45c676@hatter.bewilderbeest.net"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Tan Siewert","address":"tan@siewert.io"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Zev Weiss","address":"zev@bewilderbeest.net"}],"cc":[{"name":"Rob Herring","address":"robh@kernel.org"},{"name":"Krzysztof Kozlowski","address":"krzk+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"Conor Dooley","address":"conor+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"Joel Stanley","address":"joel@jms.id.au"},{"name":"Andrew Jeffery","address":"andrew@codeconstruct.com.au"},{"name":"","address":"devicetree@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-aspeed@lists.ozlabs.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T10:55:24.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T10:55:24.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v3 2/2] ARM: dts: aspeed: add asrock x470d4u bmc","mailingLists":[{"id":"devicetree.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"devicetree.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hi Zev,"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Many thanks for your review!"},{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On 16.08.26 06:49, Zev Weiss wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"On Wed, Aug 12, 2026 at 01:28:27PM PDT, Tan Siewert wrote:"},{"depth":2,"text":"diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u- >> data64.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u- >> data64.dts"},{"depth":2,"text":"new file mode 100644"},{"depth":2,"text":"index 000000000000..6f11aeab087c"},{"depth":2,"text":"--- /dev/null"},{"depth":2,"text":"+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u-data64.dts"},{"depth":2,"text":"@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@"},{"depth":2,"text":"+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+"},{"depth":2,"text":"+"},{"depth":2,"text":"+#include \"aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u.dts\""},{"depth":2,"text":"+"},{"depth":2,"text":"+/ {"},{"depth":2,"text":"+    compatible = \"asrock,x470d4u-data64-bmc\", \"aspeed,ast2500\";"},{"depth":2,"text":"+    model = \"Asrock Rack X470D4U-series BMC (64MB store)\";"},{"depth":1,"text":"> Nit: for consistency with how they spell it, and (at least *most* of) > the other aspeed-bmc-asrock-*.dts files, I'd suggest \"ASRock\" instead of > \"Asrock\".  (And IMO s/store/flash/ would be a touch clearer.)"},{"depth":1,"text":"Agreed on both, will fix it in v4."}],"lineCount":16,"maximumDepth":2},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Also, looks like the other nearby DTS files pretty consistently have > compatible & model in the opposite order, so matching that might be nice > too."}],"lineCount":1,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"This is something that was reported by `scripts/dtc/dt-style-check --mode strict`. Depending on how much time I have next week I'll look into fixing the dtc offsenses for arm/dts/aspeed (tho that'd come from my employer email)."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":">> +};"},{"depth":2,"text":"+"},{"depth":2,"text":"+&fmc {"},{"depth":2,"text":"+    flash@0 {"},{"depth":2,"text":"+        /delete-node/partitions;"},{"depth":2,"text":"+#include \"openbmc-flash-layout-64.dtsi\""},{"depth":2,"text":"+    };"},{"depth":2,"text":"+};"},{"depth":2,"text":"diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u.dts b/ >> arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u.dts"},{"depth":2,"text":"new file mode 100644"},{"depth":2,"text":"index 000000000000..80fb2b7c1e0c"},{"depth":2,"text":"--- /dev/null"},{"depth":2,"text":"+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x470d4u.dts"},{"depth":1,"text":"> <snip>"},{"depth":1,"text":">> +"},{"depth":2,"text":"+    fan@3 {"},{"depth":2,"text":"+        /* FAN4 (6-pin) */"},{"depth":2,"text":"+        reg = <0x03>;"},{"depth":2,"text":"+        aspeed,fan-tach-ch = /bits/ 8 <0x03 0x0b>;"},{"depth":2,"text":"+    };"},{"depth":2,"text":"+"},{"depth":2,"text":"+    fan@4 {"},{"depth":2,"text":"+        /* FAN5 (6-pin) */"},{"depth":2,"text":"+        reg = <0x04>;"},{"depth":2,"text":"+        aspeed,fan-tach-ch = /bits/ 8 <0x04 0x0d>;"},{"depth":2,"text":"+    };"},{"depth":2,"text":"+"},{"depth":2,"text":"+    fan@5 {"},{"depth":2,"text":"+        /* FAN6 (6-pin) */"},{"depth":2,"text":"+        reg = <0x05>;"},{"depth":2,"text":"+        aspeed,fan-tach-ch = /bits/ 8 <0x05 0x0e>;"},{"depth":2,"text":"+    };"},{"depth":2,"text":"+};"},{"depth":1,"text":"> Just to confirm, skipping channel 0xc here is intentional I assume? > (Most other related platforms have them contiguously numbered, but not > all, so another slight oddity wouldn't be too shocking.)"}],"lineCount":34,"maximumDepth":2},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The skip is intentional. That is what I found out during reverse engineering the SDR file in the vendor firmware."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Cheers,\nTan"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"8b7dcb07-2dfd-425f-8ff3-06114e45c676@hatter.bewilderbeest.net","parentId":"8b7dcb07-2dfd-425f-8ff3-06114e45c676@hatter.bewilderbeest.net"}},"rootIds":["8b7dcb07-2dfd-425f-8ff3-06114e45c676@hatter.bewilderbeest.net"],"childrenByParent":{"8b7dcb07-2dfd-425f-8ff3-06114e45c676@hatter.bewilderbeest.net":["4e653068-5ef1-47db-8e4e-3b535751e47f@siewert.io"]},"chronologicalIds":["8b7dcb07-2dfd-425f-8ff3-06114e45c676@hatter.bewilderbeest.net","4e653068-5ef1-47db-8e4e-3b535751e47f@siewert.io"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}